\title{UnitTrans: distributions on (0,1) via transformations of baseline laws}
\description{
Given a baseline random variable \eqn{Y} with any \code{d/p/q} functions and a
strictly monotone transformation \eqn{V = g(Y)} into (0,1), the package
derives the density, distribution and quantile functions of \eqn{V},
simulates from it, fits it by maximum likelihood, ranks many candidate
models, tests goodness of fit and runs simulation studies.
}
\details{
The density of \eqn{V} is
\deqn{f_V(v) = f_Y\{g^{-1}(v)\} \, |d g^{-1}(v) / dv|, \qquad 0 < v < 1.}
Six transformations are built in (see \code{\link[=trans_list]{trans_list()}}): \code{"rational"},
\code{"exponential"}, \code{"logit"}, \code{"tanh"}, \code{"probit"} and \code{"cloglog"}.
Baselines are referred to by name (e.g. \code{"gamma"} uses \code{\link[stats:GammaDist]{stats::dgamma()}},
\code{\link[stats:GammaDist]{stats::pgamma()}} and \code{\link[stats:GammaDist]{stats::qgamma()}}); functions are looked up on the
search path, then in \pkg{extraDistr} (if installed), then in \pkg{stats},
so user-written baselines work too.
}
